1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:00,753
Hello!

2
00:00:00,753 --> 00:00:07,090
This week you will learn to answer Part 3 questions in twenty-five to forty seconds,

3
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:10,108
and practise three pronunciation skills:

4
00:00:10,108 --> 00:00:12,900
word stress, linking, and intonation.

5
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,151
Point one:

6
00:00:15,151 --> 00:00:17,244
the O R E C framework.

7
00:00:17,244 --> 00:00:18,576
O for opinion:

8
00:00:18,576 --> 00:00:20,098
state your view.

9
00:00:20,098 --> 00:00:21,334
R for reason:

10
00:00:21,334 --> 00:00:22,476
explain why.

11
00:00:22,476 --> 00:00:23,807
E for example:

12
00:00:23,807 --> 00:00:25,329
give an example.

13
00:00:25,329 --> 00:00:26,756
C for contrast:

14
00:00:26,756 --> 00:00:28,659
give the other side.

15
00:00:28,659 --> 00:00:35,032
Speak about people and society in general, not only about yourself.

16
00:00:36,332 --> 00:00:40,844
In my view, cities should invest more in public transport.

17
00:00:44,144 --> 00:00:48,008
The main reason is that it saves people time and money.

18
00:00:51,308 --> 00:00:55,916
For instance, a worker can read on the train instead of driving.

19
00:00:59,216 --> 00:01:03,128
On the other hand, building new lines takes years.

20
00:01:06,428 --> 00:01:07,232
Point two:

21
00:01:07,232 --> 00:01:08,196
word stress.

22
00:01:08,196 --> 00:01:11,490
With the endings tion, ic, ity, and logy,

23
00:01:11,490 --> 00:01:15,990
the stress falls on the syllable just before the ending.

24
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:20,972
Stressing the wrong syllable makes the word hard to recognise.

25
00:01:22,272 --> 00:01:24,360
Photography.

26
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,926
Economic.

27
00:01:25,926 --> 00:01:27,840
Technology.

28
00:01:31,140 --> 00:01:33,873
I keep a record of my scores.

29
00:01:33,873 --> 00:01:36,324
Please record your answer.

30
00:01:39,624 --> 00:01:40,516
Point three:

31
00:01:40,516 --> 00:01:41,111
linking.

32
00:01:41,111 --> 00:01:43,787
Instead of dropping the final sound,

33
00:01:43,787 --> 00:01:47,875
link the final consonant to the vowel of the next word.

34
00:01:47,875 --> 00:01:51,517
For example, turn it off sounds like tur-ni-toff.

35
00:01:51,517 --> 00:01:55,680
Function words such as to or can are pronounced lightly.

36
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,276
Turn it off.

37
00:01:59,276 --> 00:02:00,615
Go out.

38
00:02:00,615 --> 00:02:02,146
I agree.

39
00:02:02,146 --> 00:02:03,868
Far away.

40
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,040
Point four:

41
00:02:08,040 --> 00:02:08,912
intonation.

42
00:02:08,912 --> 00:02:13,746
Use a falling tone at the end of statements and Wh-questions.

43
00:02:13,746 --> 00:02:17,074
Use a rising tone for Yes or No questions.

44
00:02:17,074 --> 00:02:23,176
A clear fall at the end of your main point makes your answer sound confident.

45
00:02:24,476 --> 00:02:25,717
Common mistakes.

46
00:02:25,717 --> 00:02:27,966
Stressing long words wrongly.

47
00:02:27,966 --> 00:02:31,533
Dropping final sounds instead of linking them.

48
00:02:31,533 --> 00:02:37,038
Saying every word equally loudly, so it sounds like one word at a time.

49
00:02:37,038 --> 00:02:41,381
And in Part 3, answering with one sentence and stopping,

50
00:02:41,381 --> 00:02:44,948
or talking for too long without a clear point.

51
00:02:46,748 --> 00:02:47,464
Quiz one:

52
00:02:47,464 --> 00:02:50,726
which syllable is stressed in generation:

53
00:02:50,726 --> 00:02:52,318
ge, ne, ra, or tion?

54
00:02:52,318 --> 00:02:53,034
Quiz two:

55
00:02:53,034 --> 00:02:59,399
in the phrase cheap, fast and reliable, does your voice rise on the first items,

56
00:02:59,399 --> 00:03:00,592
or on the last?

57
00:03:00,592 --> 00:03:01,467
Quiz three:

58
00:03:01,467 --> 00:03:05,684
roughly how many seconds should a Part 3 answer last?

59
00:03:09,984 --> 00:03:10,637
Answers.

60
00:03:10,637 --> 00:03:10,964
One:

61
00:03:10,964 --> 00:03:17,659
the syllable ra, because of the rule that words ending in tion are stressed on the

62
00:03:17,659 --> 00:03:19,373
syllable just before.

63
00:03:19,373 --> 00:03:19,700
Two:

64
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:23,701
rise on the early items and fall on the last one.

65
00:03:23,701 --> 00:03:24,191
Three:

66
00:03:24,191 --> 00:03:27,048
about twenty-five to forty seconds.

67
00:03:29,348 --> 00:03:29,888
Summary:

68
00:03:29,888 --> 00:03:34,675
use the O R E C framework, stress the right syllable, link your sounds,

69
00:03:34,675 --> 00:03:37,305
and fall at the end of your main point.

70
00:03:37,305 --> 00:03:42,025
Every day, practise shadowing for fifteen minutes with a model answer:

71
00:03:42,025 --> 00:03:47,756
listen to the slow version, repeat right after it, and then move to the normal speed.

72
00:03:47,756 --> 00:03:52,004
Then do the week nine exercises in the app and record yourself.
